law.text:
		If the judge or substitute judge of any district court:

Be a party to an action;


Be interested in the result of any action, otherwise than as resident or taxpayer of the city or county;


Be related to any party to the action as spouse, grandparent, parent, father-in-law, mother-in-law, child, grandchild, son-in-law, daughter-in-law, brother, sister, brother-in-law, sister-in-law, nephew, niece, uncle, aunt, first cousin, guardian or ward;


Be a material witness for either party to the action;


Be counsel for any party to the action;
			he shall not take cognizance thereof.
